{
  "name": "25-agent-adds-task",
  "description": "App round 2: a seat that connects on its own, with Create tasks on, adds tasks through the owner's path (UX-11). Its first task waits on the shipped model gate at task.before_ready and reaches Ready when the orchestrator passes it, with the seat as actor of every task event and its key on the completion. Its second task has only the review criterion: the app gate fails at once, the task stays in Backlog held with contract_incomplete, and the app opens A task an agent added needs its contract (UX-16), which closes when the owner cancels the task.",
  "covers": [
    "Contract decision UX-11: create_task runs add_task and complete_contract with the seat as caller and one key; task.created, task.contract_changed and task.ready name the seat as actor.",
    "Contract decisions UX-11 and RE-3: a completion after the model check carries the adding seat as actor and its key, and the check.finished as cause, inside the orchestrator's command.",
    "Contract decision UX-16 and PRD Holds, contract_incomplete: a failed gate on a task a seat added keeps the contract change, holds the task in Backlog and opens agent_task_incomplete, which closes with the hold when the task is cancelled."
  ],
